# Moodle PHPCS: inline comment capitalization

This recurs often in ArtQTML. Moodle coding style requires **new** `//` comments to start with an **uppercase** letter. In this plugin, PHPCS **warnings fail CI** (`phpcs.xml` has no `ignore_warnings_on_exit`).

## Do

```php
// The moodleform::$_form property is protected; assert against the definition.
// Seed the same file install and upgrade use.
```

## Do not

```php
// moodleform::$_form is protected; ...
// must stay out of the schema enum ...
```

## Rules of thumb

1. If the `//` line starts a **new** comment (not a wrap of the previous line), the first word must be capitalized.
2. Do not start a new comment with a lowercase class/method/variable name — rephrase: *"The `foo` method …"* / *"Call `bar()` …"*.
3. Mid-paragraph continuation lines may stay lowercase (they continue the sentence above).
4. GPL file-header boilerplate is exempt (standard Moodle header).
5. After writing PHP, prefer phrasing comments so a fresh `//` never begins with `[a-z]`.

When fixing CI: search for the reported file:line and capitalize or rephrase that comment — do not weaken the PHPCS gate.
